    "According to the published World Creole Music Festival 2026 guides, notably writeups24, Nice plays Night 3, on Sunday October 25, 2026. The festival runs at Windsor Park Sports Stadium in Roseau from Friday October 23 to Sunday October 25, 2026, during Dominica Independence season, under the theme “Pulsating Rhythms”. It is the 26th edition of the festival, according to the same guides. The closing night brings together, again according to writeups24, Machel Montano, Uncle Waffles, FRIDAYY, Maxi Priest, Diblo Dibala, Les Aiglons, Jean Marc Ferdinand, <a href=\"/en/shelly.html\">Shelly</a> and The Signal Band, <a href=\"/en/gwada-g.html\">Gwada G</a>, Unstoppable Shax, Nice and <a href=\"/en/dj-taffy.html\">DJ Taffy</a>.",
    "Reading that bill closely shows the coherence of the path of Nice. He meets there Shelly and Signal Band, his partners on “Bye to de Old Me”, Unstoppable Shax, his partner on “Without You”, and DJ Taffy, the producer of “Situationship”. His documented discography and his festival bill therefore tell the same story: an artist built through collaborations, booked on the night when his collaborators also play. Few emerging artist profiles offer such a clear match between studio credits and the big stage. It is one of the reasons why Bouyon Shattaz documents Nice now, rather than waiting for a solo hit to make his name unavoidable.",
    "Night 3 is the closing night, and closing WCMF carries a particular weight. The festival is Dominica great Creole showcase, the moment when Roseau presents its music to the world during Independence season. According to the Discover Dominica Authority release, the 2025 edition had drawn more than 42,000 people across its three nights. Playing the last night of the following edition, in front of that crowd, alongside international headliners and historic Creole bands, places Nice inside the official landscape of his island in the most concrete sense: his name is printed on the programme Dominica shows the world.",
    "This profile attributes that information as it should: the make-up of the nights comes from the published guides, writeups24 first, and the confirmation of the Dominican artists comes from the Discover Dominica Authority release. If the official programme were to change, this page would be corrected and dated, like every page on this site. In the meantime, the listening advice is simple: prepare for Night 3 by hearing “Bye to de Old Me” in both its versions, then “Without You”, in our <a href=\"/en/playlist-bouyon.html\">bouyon playlist</a> and on the <a href=\"/en/shelly.html\">Shelly</a> and <a href=\"/en/signal-band.html\">Signal Band</a> pages."
